# Local Yocto builds — lower priority than desktop

Local **kas-container**, **bitbake**, and related Yocto/LmP builds are long-running and CPU/IO heavy. They must **not** compete with interactive desktop work on the same machine.

## Agent behavior

When starting or suggesting local Yocto builds, **always** use lower scheduling priority:

```bash
nice -n 15 ionice -c2 -n7 kas-container ... build kas/imx95-frdm-evk-mfgtool.yml
```

Prefer `./scripts/kas-build-lowprio.sh` from `android-container/` when invoking kas from this repo.

## Defaults

| Tool | Setting | Meaning |
|------|---------|---------|
| `nice` | **10–19** (default **15**) | Lower CPU priority vs normal (0) |
| `ionice` | **`-c 2 -n 7`** | Best-effort class, idle/lowest I/O priority |

Override via env: `NICE_LEVEL`, `IONICE_CLASS`, `IONICE_LEVEL`.

## Already running builds

If bitbake was started without nice/ionice, lower priority in place:

```bash
renice -n 15 -p $(pgrep -f '[b]itbake')
ionice -c2 -n7 -p $(pgrep -f '[b]itbake')
```

## Scope

Applies to local developer machines only — **not** CI runners or dedicated build servers where full CPU/IO is intended.
